          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong exterior algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            of a vector space is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded-commutative+algebra"} graded-commutative algebra
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            are taken to be of degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            takes a graded-commutative algebra to its vector space of degree-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            elements.)
          %p
            This construction generalizes to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+representations"} group representations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear categories
            with enough
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimits
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rig"} 2-rig
          %h2#explicit_definition Explicit definition
          %p We begin with the construction for vector spaces and then sketch how to generalize it.
          %h3#for_vector_spaces For vector spaces
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %strong exterior algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            is generated by the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            using these operations:
          %ul
            %li addition and scalar multiplication
            %li
              an associative binary operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
              called the
              %strong exterior product
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %strong wedge product
          %p subject to these identities:
          %ul
            %li
              the identities necessary for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
              to be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            %li
              the identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \wedge v = 0
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
          %p
            It then follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi p
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^p V
            is spanned by
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1 \wedge \cdots \wedge v_p
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_1, \dots, v_p \in V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutative+algebra"} graded commutative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi p
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Lambda^p V
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi q
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu \in \Lambda^q V
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ν
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ν
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \wedge \nu = (-1)^{p q}\, \nu \wedge \omega
              \.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is a field not of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          #eq:alternating.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \wedge v = 0
          %p by the relations
          #eq:antisymmetric.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \wedge w = - w \wedge v
          %p
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v, w \in V
            (
            %a{:href => "#Grassmann1844"}> Grassmann 1844, §37, §55
            ). If we can divide by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:antisymmetric"} (2)
            imply
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:alternating"} (1)
          %p
            The exterior algebra of a vector space is also called the
            %strong Grassmann algebra
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong alternating algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigwedge^\bullet V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alt
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alt V
          %h3#in_general In general
          %p
            More generally, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in C
            is any object. Then we can form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor powers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has countable coproducts we can form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T V = \bigoplus_{n \ge 0} V^{\otimes n}
          %p
            (which we write here as a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T V
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            object in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi p
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi q
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes p} \otimes V^{\otimes q} \to V^{\otimes (p+q)}
          %p
            This monoid object is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            acts on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{\otimes n}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear category
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            zero, then we can form the antisymmetrization map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A : V^{\otimes n} \to V^{\otimes n}
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                  %mi sgn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_A = \frac{1}{n!} \sum_{\sigma \in S_n} sgn(\sigma) \, \sigma
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 - p_A
            is called the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %strong antisymmetric tensor power
            or
            %strong alternating power
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi n
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^n V
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi n
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V = \bigoplus_{n \ge 0} \Lambda^n V
          %p
            becomes a monoid object called the
            %strong exterior algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a linear category over a field of positive characteristic (or more generally, over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            in which not every positive integer is invertible, that is which is not itself an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            over the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi n
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^n V
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#over_a_super_vector_space Over a super vector space
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            is often called the
            %strong Grassmann algebra
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda V
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+algebra"} graded commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            Explicitly, this is the quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T V
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            generated by elements of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi w
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mi v
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi deg
                      %mi w
                  %mi w
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \otimes w + (-1)^{deg v \cdot deg w } w \otimes v \, .
          %p
            The product in this algebra is denoted with a wedge, and called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong wedge product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mi v
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi deg
                      %mi w
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  v \wedge w = - (-1)^{deg v \cdot deg w} w \wedge v
                  \\,.
          %h4#with_an_inner_product With an inner product
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
            then there is also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p But sometimes it is useful to consider the Grassmann algebra even in the presence of a non-degenerate bilinear form, in which case the inner product still serves to induce identifications between elements of the Grassmann algebra in different degree.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^3
            equipped with its standard inner product. Then an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 0
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^0 V
            is a scalar (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 1
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^1 V
            may be identified with a vector in the elementary sense, an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 2
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^2 V
            may be identified with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bivector"} bivector
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudovector"} pseudovector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mn 3
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^3 V
            may be identified a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoscalar"} pseudoscalar
          %p
            More generally, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi p
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^p V
            is a
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+algebra"} geometric algebra
            = succeed "-vectors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-pseudovectors." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-p)
          %p
            On a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*X
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda T^*X
            using the abstract nonsense describe earlier, taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundles
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the vector bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda T^*X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an oriented (semi)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"}> Riemannian manifold
            , then we can identify
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-forms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-p)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star"} Hodge star
            operator.
          %h3#semifree_dgalgebras Semi-free dg-algebras
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semi-free dg-algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            whose underlying graded commutative algebra is free, i.e. is an exterior algebra. Examples include in particular
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} algebras
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie ∞-algebroids
          %h4#differential_forms__derham_complex Differential forms / deRham complex
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            consider the category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            of smooth functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(X) = \Gamma(T^* X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+complex"} deRham complex
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the exterior algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋀
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet(X) = \bigwedge_{C^\infty(X)} \Gamma(T^* X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is really a special case of the previous class of examples, as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
            equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+complex"} deRham differential
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
